                <pb facs="0850" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/12–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sands</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-07T16:00:00+03:06">December 7, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>404. In audience for entire Diplomatic Corps Thursday King Abdul Aziz said he
                    wished it clearly understood that his moderation on Palestine question was due
                    entirely to his disinclination for a misunderstanding with America and Britain
                    and not to fear of Jews or Change in categorical attitude.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept as 404, repeated Cairo for Eddy as 281.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sands</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
